# Crag SHADOW that NEUTRALIZES the packaged 'chrony' waitsync gate
# (cports/main/chrony/files/chrony, shipped ENABLED by chrony-dinit:
# chronyc waitsync 180 … before time-sync.target). On an appliance that
# may legitimately live offline, that gate holds boot — and the
# boot-smoke budget — for up to 180 s every single boot. Crag's
# time story does not need it (docs/07 §6): the build-epoch floor makes
# the clock sane before NTP, cragd exposes time.synced for anyone who
# must wait, and TLS-gated work checks synced-or-past-floor itself.
#
# Kept as a service (not just disabled) because the packaged enable
# symlink lives in chrony-dinit's boot.d; shadowing the NAME is the
# reliable override, exactly like the iwd shadow. time-sync.target is
# therefore reached immediately — services that truly need synced time
# must consult cragd, not the target.

type = scripted
command = /usr/bin/true
before: time-sync.target
depends-on: chronyd
